1
00:00:00,383 --> 00:00:02,053
(Child actors were accompanied by a guardian...)

2
00:00:02,123 --> 00:00:03,793
(and filmed in a safe, supervised environment.)

3
00:00:05,663 --> 00:00:07,193
What did you just say?

4
00:00:07,933 --> 00:00:10,093
Are you asking me for a divorce?

5
00:00:11,563 --> 00:00:13,563
Yes. Let's get a divorce.

6
00:00:14,033 --> 00:00:16,403
- Dad. - Seriously, what's gotten into you?

7
00:00:17,133 --> 00:00:19,943
Seong Mi. He's had a little too much to drink.

8
00:00:20,343 --> 00:00:24,013
- It's just the alcohol talking. - It's not. I'm serious.

9
00:00:24,573 --> 00:00:27,913
- Jeong Han. - How can you start this?

10
00:00:28,213 --> 00:00:29,653
As if you've done nothing wrong.

11
00:00:30,113 --> 00:00:33,123
Fine. I haven't done anything right. That's why I want a divorce.

12
00:00:33,483 --> 00:00:36,693
And even if I put myself in your shoes,

13
00:00:37,093 --> 00:00:38,663
you're too good for me.

14
00:00:38,923 --> 00:00:42,693
Besides, didn't you say you regret marrying me?

15
00:00:44,563 --> 00:00:47,103
How could you say that in front of Mother?

16
00:00:47,633 --> 00:00:49,403
You can't say it in front of my mom,

17
00:00:49,873 --> 00:00:51,443
so I'm saying it for you.

18
00:00:52,403 --> 00:00:53,443
Jeong Han.

19
00:00:53,703 --> 00:00:56,413
I know you're drunk, but still. How could you say that?

20
00:00:56,643 --> 00:00:57,673
In front of Woo Jae.

21
00:00:59,043 --> 00:01:01,143
Seong Mi, it looks like something happened to him.

22
00:01:02,053 --> 00:01:04,613
Hey, where on earth did you drink so much?

23
00:01:07,453 --> 00:01:10,693
At Mr. Go Il Sik's funeral.

24
00:01:11,363 --> 00:01:12,363
What?

25
00:01:13,063 --> 00:01:14,563
Wait, that gentleman...

26
00:01:15,993 --> 00:01:17,133
He passed away?

27
00:01:17,433 --> 00:01:18,433
Yes.

28
00:01:19,133 --> 00:01:21,733
I waited for his family to arrive and for the wake to be set up,

29
00:01:23,533 --> 00:01:25,273
and I had a few drinks at the funeral home.

30
00:01:25,703 --> 00:01:26,773
I'm sorry.

31
00:01:27,503 --> 00:01:30,213
Then you should have called and told us.

32
00:01:30,443 --> 00:01:34,383
Seong Mi, that's what happened. If you could just...

33
00:01:35,583 --> 00:01:36,953
be a little understanding...

34
00:01:37,653 --> 00:01:40,283
Right. I should be understanding.

35
00:01:40,923 --> 00:01:42,753
So I'm the only one who has to be understanding. Is that it?

36
00:01:45,263 --> 00:01:47,693
Here you go again, making me out to be the bad guy.

37
00:01:48,833 --> 00:01:51,163
I'm the villain who's always...

38
00:01:51,163 --> 00:01:53,203
picking on poor, innocent you, right?

39
00:01:55,933 --> 00:01:56,973
No...

40
00:02:10,813 --> 00:02:11,923
Dad.

41
00:02:23,563 --> 00:02:26,063
Oh, honey. That's not going to do it.

42
00:02:26,833 --> 00:02:29,773
Just throw everything until you feel better.

43
00:02:33,043 --> 00:02:34,573
That man who passed away...

44
00:02:35,643 --> 00:02:38,613
Jeong Han saved his life a few years ago.

45
00:02:39,383 --> 00:02:42,383
He was always so worried about him,

46
00:02:42,383 --> 00:02:44,113
so it's a real shame this happened.

47
00:02:46,123 --> 00:02:47,153
I know.

48
00:02:47,783 --> 00:02:49,423
I know exactly how he feels, but...

49
00:02:50,453 --> 00:02:51,923
I know how you feel, too.

50
00:02:52,723 --> 00:02:56,633
He said that because he's drunk. Just forget you heard it, okay?

51
00:02:58,133 --> 00:02:59,303
I'm sorry.

52
00:03:00,133 --> 00:03:03,703
Mother, why do you always apologise for our mistakes?

53
00:03:04,973 --> 00:03:06,103
I do?

54
00:03:06,243 --> 00:03:09,513
Because you do this, I always end up forgiving him.

55
00:03:09,973 --> 00:03:14,113
And what if you don't? Are you really going to split up?

56
00:03:15,253 --> 00:03:16,583
How could I?

57
00:03:17,353 --> 00:03:18,683
I have nowhere else to go.

58
00:03:19,183 --> 00:03:21,723
I don't have a family to go back to, or a mother of my own.

59
00:03:22,153 --> 00:03:25,263
You're my mother. Where am I supposed to go?

60
00:03:29,293 --> 00:03:30,763
- Dad, come on. - Let go of me.

61
00:03:30,763 --> 00:03:32,533
- Come on, let's go. - Hey!

62
00:03:32,603 --> 00:03:34,003
- Hurry up. - Oh, for crying out loud.

63
00:03:36,273 --> 00:03:38,073
If anyone's leaving, it should be him.

64
00:03:39,473 --> 00:03:40,573
Exactly.

65
00:03:41,473 --> 00:03:44,443
Hey, you better straighten up, or you'll be the one kicked out.

66
00:03:49,283 --> 00:03:50,283
What?

67
00:03:52,653 --> 00:03:54,823
I'm sorry.

68
00:04:04,563 --> 00:04:06,803
I'm thinking of growing it out.

69
00:04:06,903 --> 00:04:10,173
- You'd look pretty either way. - This is my hair without bangs.

70
00:04:13,273 --> 00:04:15,373
I was so sure there was something between them.

71
00:04:17,773 --> 00:04:22,253
Your brother and Seong Mi made up. They're all talk.

72
00:04:22,453 --> 00:04:24,283
I don't think they're actually getting a divorce.

73
00:04:25,353 --> 00:04:26,353
I hope not.

74
00:04:28,553 --> 00:04:31,763
I'm sorry for mentioning the deposit to Seong Mi.

75
00:04:32,963 --> 00:04:36,863
I only did it because I was mad that you were being mean to me.

76
00:04:38,133 --> 00:04:39,263
So...

77
00:04:40,203 --> 00:04:42,203
it's your turn to apologise to me.

78
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:45,773
Apologise. To me.

79
00:04:49,873 --> 00:04:50,913
I'm sorry.

80
00:04:51,783 --> 00:04:53,983
I just lost my temper because I was angry about my uncle.

81
00:04:55,813 --> 00:04:59,083
I figured. Your uncle is a real piece of work, isn't he?

82
00:05:02,323 --> 00:05:04,293
Mother's calling. Hurry up and come out.

83
00:05:09,893 --> 00:05:11,493
Was I mistaken?

84
00:05:12,863 --> 00:05:14,803
I don't think she's cheating on me after all.

85
00:05:21,303 --> 00:05:23,913
We are going to keep holding the memorial every year.

86
00:05:25,013 --> 00:05:27,413
I do not want people saying I am neglecting my duties...

87
00:05:27,413 --> 00:05:28,553
now that my husband is gone.

88
00:05:29,283 --> 00:05:32,983
But I'll take care of it on my own, simply and quietly.

89
00:05:33,323 --> 00:05:34,993
So, you guys don't need to worry about it anymore.

90
00:05:38,693 --> 00:05:39,693
And...

91
00:05:40,363 --> 00:05:42,963
a family shouldn't go to bed angry at each other.

92
00:05:43,533 --> 00:05:45,503
Let's all make up before we go to sleep, okay?

93
00:05:46,533 --> 00:05:49,303
We already made up in our room, Mother.

94
00:05:51,773 --> 00:05:53,243
Seong Mi, please don't be upset anymore.

95
00:05:54,173 --> 00:05:58,213
I don't regret using our security deposit to help...

96
00:05:58,443 --> 00:05:59,543
with your clinic.

97
00:06:00,083 --> 00:06:01,483
She means it, Seong Mi.

98
00:06:04,413 --> 00:06:05,423
I think...

99
00:06:05,853 --> 00:06:08,253
I'm about to land another show.

100
00:06:09,193 --> 00:06:10,193
Really?

101
00:06:10,893 --> 00:06:14,023
As soon as I get the advance, we will pay the salaries first.

102
00:06:15,293 --> 00:06:16,493
That's great news!

103
00:06:16,833 --> 00:06:19,163
We couldn't even make our savings deposit this month.

104
00:06:20,003 --> 00:06:22,333
Mom, it feels like you're taking on too much work.

105
00:06:23,433 --> 00:06:26,503
He's right. You're already so busy. Aren't you doing too much?

106
00:06:27,203 --> 00:06:30,043
No, it's fine. You know I was made for TV.

107
00:06:30,243 --> 00:06:31,413
It's actually pretty fun.

108
00:06:31,843 --> 00:06:34,113
Good. You're staying the night, right?

109
00:06:34,613 --> 00:06:35,613
Sorry?

110
00:06:36,283 --> 00:06:40,053
- Well... - Yes. Mom, you should stay over.

111
00:06:40,483 --> 00:06:43,293
That's right. Especially now, you two should be sharing a room.

112
00:06:43,953 --> 00:06:45,323
Sharing a room?

113
00:06:47,463 --> 00:06:48,593
You're going to sleep in my room?

114
00:06:49,293 --> 00:06:51,263
I'm sleeping in Ju Ah's room.

115
00:06:52,103 --> 00:06:56,073
Woo Jae. Have you heard from Ju Ah?

116
00:06:56,433 --> 00:06:59,673
- No. Her phone's still off. - Dear...

117
00:07:00,573 --> 00:07:02,813
She must be really upset.

118
00:07:03,413 --> 00:07:05,913
For sure. After being humiliated like that.

119
00:07:06,283 --> 00:07:09,583
- Still, she's not coming home? - What's wrong now?

120
00:07:09,883 --> 00:07:11,683
Is something wrong with Ju Ah?

121
00:07:16,593 --> 00:07:18,193
Why? What?

122
00:07:20,723 --> 00:07:22,533
My existence...

123
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:28,603
wasn't the fruit of their love, but just a mistake!

124
00:07:31,373 --> 00:07:32,503
It was like...

125
00:07:33,443 --> 00:07:37,643
I've spent my whole life feeling abandoned, I guess?

126
00:07:41,753 --> 00:07:44,313
That's why I tried to work so much harder.

127
00:07:44,753 --> 00:07:49,323
More than anyone, I just wanted my parents' approval.

128
00:07:51,153 --> 00:07:52,263
But today,

129
00:07:53,063 --> 00:07:57,763
I just crashed and burned spectacularly.

130
00:07:58,563 --> 00:08:00,603
I can't even go home.

131
00:08:05,843 --> 00:08:10,043
I wish I'd never been born...

132
00:08:19,353 --> 00:08:23,253
I should've just never been born.

133
00:08:29,333 --> 00:08:30,333
What?

134
00:08:31,593 --> 00:08:32,833
My teddy bear.

135
00:08:33,363 --> 00:08:35,773
Teddy, where are you going?

136
00:08:36,173 --> 00:08:40,943
- Hey, I didn't abandon you. Oh, no. - What?

137
00:08:44,813 --> 00:08:45,843
Don't tell me...

138
00:08:46,583 --> 00:08:48,343
The person it happened to...

139
00:08:48,953 --> 00:08:52,953
could be so humiliated they want to die, you know?

140
00:08:55,953 --> 00:08:57,623
(Danger: Sudden Deep Water Fatal Accidents Have Occurred)

141
00:08:57,693 --> 00:08:58,863
(Fatal Accidents Have Occurred)

142
00:09:00,523 --> 00:09:01,693
Darn it, seriously...

143
00:09:02,093 --> 00:09:03,233
Hey, you!

144
00:09:09,433 --> 00:09:10,603
Are you trying to kill yourself?

145
00:09:12,673 --> 00:09:13,743
Me?

146
00:09:15,373 --> 00:09:19,143
- You're not, right? - Of course not. Why would I?

147
00:09:19,813 --> 00:09:22,283
I'm still alive and kicking!

148
00:09:24,483 --> 00:09:25,523
Right.

149
00:09:26,823 --> 00:09:28,753
You're not dead, but you sure are drunk.

150
00:09:29,353 --> 00:09:30,853
But you...

151
00:09:31,223 --> 00:09:33,363
Have you been following me this whole time?

152
00:09:34,063 --> 00:09:37,033
Darn it, are you some kind of pervert?

153
00:09:37,163 --> 00:09:38,263
A pervert?

154
00:09:39,533 --> 00:09:41,463
- No, I'm not. - Whatever.

155
00:09:41,833 --> 00:09:43,233
Don't come any closer.

156
00:09:44,633 --> 00:09:47,273
Fine. Get out of the water. I'll help you.

157
00:09:47,403 --> 00:09:51,743
Hey! What, so you can grab me? Stay away.

158
00:09:51,813 --> 00:09:56,453
- This is a warning. - Gosh, okay. I won't grab you.

159
00:09:57,653 --> 00:09:58,883
- Oh, no! - Good grief.

160
00:10:04,023 --> 00:10:05,363
Gosh, that scared me.

161
00:10:10,263 --> 00:10:11,763
Hey, my hand...

162
00:10:17,503 --> 00:10:20,643
I'm going to die! Help... Help me!

163
00:10:20,943 --> 00:10:23,143
Help me! Please, help me! I'm going to die...

164
00:10:37,293 --> 00:10:38,923
You really won't help me?

165
00:10:39,063 --> 00:10:42,233
You said you'd call the cops on me as a pervert if I grabbed you.

166
00:10:42,563 --> 00:10:46,933
Well... Who goes around following someone...

167
00:10:47,003 --> 00:10:48,433
in the middle of the night like this?

168
00:10:49,233 --> 00:10:50,233
Unbelievable.

169
00:11:17,463 --> 00:11:18,633
Why are you following me?

170
00:11:18,933 --> 00:11:20,833
Are you some kind of pervert?

171
00:11:23,503 --> 00:11:26,703
Well, I'm so sorry to ask,

172
00:11:27,173 --> 00:11:29,313
but my phone got wet,

173
00:11:29,313 --> 00:11:31,413
so I can't call or look anything up.

174
00:11:32,613 --> 00:11:35,953
And of course, my mobile pay isn't working either.

175
00:11:39,483 --> 00:11:42,553
If you could let me make one call, I swear I'll make it up to you.

176
00:11:47,793 --> 00:11:48,793
Here.

177
00:11:49,463 --> 00:11:51,763
Thank you so much. Really.

178
00:11:56,103 --> 00:11:57,803
What? What was it?

179
00:11:58,233 --> 00:12:01,643
Woo Jae's number... Zero, one, zero, three, two, three?

180
00:12:02,043 --> 00:12:03,343
Three, two, two, zero?

181
00:12:03,873 --> 00:12:04,873
No, that's not it.

182
00:12:05,513 --> 00:12:07,283
Darn it. This is driving me crazy. What was it?

183
00:12:07,743 --> 00:12:09,153
You can't remember the number?

184
00:12:10,183 --> 00:12:11,353
Not even your home number?

185
00:12:11,483 --> 00:12:13,583
Well...

186
00:12:23,593 --> 00:12:24,633
Welcome.

187
00:12:25,333 --> 00:12:27,033
Sorry, I'm late.

188
00:12:27,233 --> 00:12:30,473
You sure are. I had everything ready and thought you weren't coming.

189
00:12:30,633 --> 00:12:31,733
How could I not?

190
00:12:32,043 --> 00:12:34,203
The Seonpo-ri Gaetdari Samhap Meal...

191
00:12:34,403 --> 00:12:36,373
from Episode 81 of "Everyday Meals Across Korea."

192
00:12:36,573 --> 00:12:39,013
I've been waiting for this since I booked it two months ago.

193
00:12:40,443 --> 00:12:42,513
But there are two of you.

194
00:12:42,813 --> 00:12:45,113
But you only booked the guesthouse package for one.

195
00:12:45,113 --> 00:12:48,423
Oh, well... It's a long story.

196
00:12:48,653 --> 00:12:53,263
- Do you have any spare rooms? - No, we're all booked for tonight.

197
00:12:53,363 --> 00:12:54,393
I see.

198
00:12:54,693 --> 00:12:58,293
I booked the rooftop too, so I guess I can sleep there.

199
00:13:02,003 --> 00:13:03,333
Go on in, wash up, and get some sleep.

200
00:13:06,273 --> 00:13:08,273
- Thank you. - Sure.

201
00:13:19,483 --> 00:13:21,823
Here, change into these.

202
00:13:23,323 --> 00:13:24,393
And...

203
00:13:25,393 --> 00:13:26,563
Make sure you lock the door.

204
00:13:27,623 --> 00:13:29,863
You never know. There might be a pervert lurking.

205
00:13:34,033 --> 00:13:35,033
The nerve of him...

206
00:13:46,313 --> 00:13:49,313
Come on. Please turn on.

207
00:13:54,723 --> 00:13:56,793
It won't turn on.

208
00:14:02,933 --> 00:14:04,133
I smell meat.

209
00:14:14,503 --> 00:14:15,513
Hey.

210
00:14:16,113 --> 00:14:18,543
- Feeling a little more sober? - Yes.

211
00:14:21,643 --> 00:14:26,153
Apparently, you can see the mudflats and the moonlight here at once.

212
00:14:26,223 --> 00:14:27,523
That's why they call it the Gaetdari Garden.

213
00:14:28,323 --> 00:14:29,523
I see.

214
00:14:29,853 --> 00:14:32,193
- Have a seat. - Okay.

215
00:14:38,963 --> 00:14:42,773
You hardly touched your duck. Have some. It's Gaetdari Samhap.

216
00:14:44,603 --> 00:14:46,703
- Okay. - Here. This is...

217
00:14:46,773 --> 00:14:48,703
- I really shouldn't... - Hair of the dog.

218
00:14:49,543 --> 00:14:54,113
The owner brews it himself with rice grown in the sea breeze.

219
00:14:54,283 --> 00:14:56,113
I see.

220
00:14:56,853 --> 00:14:59,623
All right. You take this aged kimchi,

221
00:14:59,923 --> 00:15:03,153
put some perfectly cooked brisket on top,

222
00:15:03,693 --> 00:15:08,593
top it with scallop and abalone, roll it all up,

223
00:15:08,763 --> 00:15:13,103
and dip it in this sauce made from plum syrup! Like this.

224
00:15:14,603 --> 00:15:15,773
All right then.

225
00:15:25,073 --> 00:15:27,183
- Incredible. - It's amazing, right?

226
00:15:27,483 --> 00:15:32,013
The brisket's savoury fat mellows out the acidity of the aged kimchi.

227
00:15:32,083 --> 00:15:35,653
Then just as the sweetness of the scallop washes over you,

228
00:15:35,723 --> 00:15:40,363
the sauce comes in with a kick. Then, a sip of this makgeolli.

229
00:15:40,693 --> 00:15:41,693
Oh, yes.

230
00:15:46,563 --> 00:15:48,833
The perfect finishing touch.

231
00:15:49,673 --> 00:15:53,173
You really know your food. Hold on. I'll make you another one.

232
00:15:59,513 --> 00:16:03,853
You seem to be on vacation. I'm so sorry for ruining it for you.

233
00:16:04,713 --> 00:16:08,653
I made a huge mistake today and lost my job.

234
00:16:08,723 --> 00:16:11,123
But I just couldn't bring myself to go home,

235
00:16:11,893 --> 00:16:14,763
so I just hopped on the first bus that came along,

236
00:16:14,823 --> 00:16:17,363
and I guess I zoned out and ended up here at the last stop.

237
00:16:18,793 --> 00:16:23,403
I'm really not like this at all. I don't know what's gotten into me.

238
00:16:23,703 --> 00:16:27,103
I've been a mess, making mistakes and causing so much trouble...

239
00:16:27,873 --> 00:16:29,143
I'm so sorry.

240
00:16:29,273 --> 00:16:33,383
It happens. We all have those days when it feels like you're in a fog.

241
00:16:34,843 --> 00:16:38,253
In Spain, if someone makes many mistakes,

242
00:16:38,853 --> 00:16:41,583
people say, "Oh, they must be in love."

243
00:16:42,423 --> 00:16:46,123
But Koreans are a little tough on mistakes, aren't they?

244
00:16:47,223 --> 00:16:49,133
Thank you for being so understanding.

245
00:16:52,403 --> 00:16:53,403
What?

246
00:16:53,403 --> 00:16:57,273
I said I had fun today. I'm okay, so please cheer up.

247
00:16:58,803 --> 00:16:59,873
Thank you.

248
00:17:09,953 --> 00:17:13,323
Weren't you sleeping in Ju Ah's room?

249
00:17:13,323 --> 00:17:14,583
The door's locked.

250
00:17:15,323 --> 00:17:17,323
What? So, you're going to sleep here?

251
00:17:17,693 --> 00:17:19,163
What, you want me to sleep out in the hall?

252
00:17:20,293 --> 00:17:21,893
No, I'll go sleep somewhere else then.

253
00:17:22,223 --> 00:17:23,993
Just sleep here.

254
00:17:24,293 --> 00:17:27,103
If not, your mother will worry that we've been fighting again.

255
00:17:27,863 --> 00:17:29,473
Good grief.

256
00:17:32,133 --> 00:17:34,403
What are you waiting for? Go and wash up.

257
00:17:34,703 --> 00:17:35,713
What?

258
00:17:36,443 --> 00:17:37,673
You want me to wash up?

259
00:17:38,143 --> 00:17:39,583
Were you not going to?

260
00:17:39,743 --> 00:17:40,783
No.

261
00:17:41,183 --> 00:17:44,183
No, I mean... Of course, I will. I'll go wash up.

262
00:17:50,123 --> 00:17:52,723
But why would she tell me to wash up?

263
00:17:53,563 --> 00:17:55,423
It's kind of scaring me.

264
00:18:07,243 --> 00:18:08,303
What's this about?

265
00:18:15,343 --> 00:18:19,083
- You think you're sleeping here? - Where else am I supposed to sleep?

266
00:18:19,423 --> 00:18:21,853
Sleep on the floor. I already put out your bedding.

267
00:18:22,023 --> 00:18:25,053
I can't sleep on the floor. My back will kill me.

268
00:18:25,123 --> 00:18:26,863
So you expect me to sleep on the floor?

269
00:18:27,023 --> 00:18:29,893
What's the big deal? Why is it okay for me, but not you?

270
00:18:30,363 --> 00:18:31,693
You're being so childish.

271
00:18:34,033 --> 00:18:36,103
- Fine, rock-paper-scissors for it. - Forget it.

272
00:18:36,403 --> 00:18:38,003
Talk about childish.

273
00:18:38,273 --> 00:18:40,903
Seriously, if this was the plan, why did you even tell me to wash up?

274
00:18:41,873 --> 00:18:45,443
You should wash up before bed. You won't do it unless I say so.

275
00:18:45,643 --> 00:18:47,583
A doctor, of all people, being so unhygienic.

276
00:18:47,683 --> 00:18:49,253
I wash up before work, okay?

277
00:18:49,253 --> 00:18:51,683
And it's not like I treat patients with my body.

278
00:18:52,683 --> 00:18:56,523
But what's with you asking why I told you to wash up?

279
00:18:57,423 --> 00:18:59,063
What exactly were you expecting?

280
00:18:59,863 --> 00:19:02,963
What do you mean, expecting? I wasn't expecting anything.

281
00:19:03,233 --> 00:19:06,633
My gosh. You think I want to sleep in the same room as you?

282
00:19:06,703 --> 00:19:09,733
You snore like a freight train, you know. Unbelievable.

283
00:19:09,803 --> 00:19:11,003
You're going to sleep in those clothes?

284
00:19:11,633 --> 00:19:13,173
Gosh, whatever. It's too much trouble.

285
00:19:14,943 --> 00:19:19,113
If you ever mention divorce again in front of your mother,

286
00:19:19,183 --> 00:19:20,243
you'll regret it.

287
00:19:20,883 --> 00:19:22,453
Fine, I get it.

288
00:19:26,123 --> 00:19:29,023
The more I think about it, the more ridiculous it is.

289
00:19:30,353 --> 00:19:34,323
What? You'll grant me a divorce because I look miserable?

290
00:19:35,833 --> 00:19:37,293
Let's just get some sleep.

291
00:19:37,633 --> 00:19:40,333
You pretend to be the nice guy who's putting up with everything,

292
00:19:40,463 --> 00:19:43,873
but you just make me uncomfortable. That's being passive-aggressive.

293
00:19:44,173 --> 00:19:46,973
Passive-aggressive behaviour, to use the technical term.

294
00:19:49,813 --> 00:19:52,273
Gosh, I can't even stand the sight of him.

295
00:19:56,483 --> 00:19:58,113
- Cheers! - Hey.

296
00:20:03,823 --> 00:20:05,653
Oh, this is nice.

297
00:20:07,023 --> 00:20:08,123
Oh, boy.

298
00:20:08,623 --> 00:20:09,863
Man...

299
00:20:11,693 --> 00:20:12,763
By the way,

300
00:20:13,633 --> 00:20:15,203
about that wardrobe malfunction on the shopping network.

301
00:20:16,603 --> 00:20:17,873
You said it was a simple mistake, right?

302
00:20:19,303 --> 00:20:21,243
Then why can't you go back to work?

303
00:20:21,673 --> 00:20:24,513
Because you're too embarrassed about it?

304
00:20:25,883 --> 00:20:30,313
Because I feel like I don't deserve to design clothes anymore.

305
00:20:31,853 --> 00:20:32,883
I...

306
00:20:33,483 --> 00:20:37,753
was actually relieved that it happened to me.

307
00:20:38,723 --> 00:20:42,593
One of my customers could have gone through that, you know?

308
00:20:43,263 --> 00:20:47,803
I could have ruined someone's wonderful day.

309
00:20:49,833 --> 00:20:51,033
You know,

310
00:20:51,533 --> 00:20:53,573
I love seeing people happy in the clothes I make.

311
00:20:53,803 --> 00:20:57,513
I love making people happy.

312
00:20:59,983 --> 00:21:01,113
That's admirable.

313
00:21:02,083 --> 00:21:04,983
Someone who creates happiness.

314
00:21:08,983 --> 00:21:12,253
"Someone who creates happiness."

315
00:21:16,333 --> 00:21:17,833
But why can't you go home?

316
00:21:18,333 --> 00:21:21,233
Isn't family who you're supposed to lean on during tough times?

317
00:21:23,603 --> 00:21:28,343
My whole family will be there today for my great-grandfather's memorial.

318
00:21:28,703 --> 00:21:31,573
And it's obvious what happened to me will be the main topic of gossip.

319
00:21:36,113 --> 00:21:38,113
That sounds nice, actually. Like a real, lively family.

320
00:21:41,553 --> 00:21:43,023
What's your family like?

321
00:21:47,593 --> 00:21:48,863
I don't know.

322
00:21:55,563 --> 00:21:59,243
My parents divorced when I was a kid.

323
00:22:00,403 --> 00:22:05,113
My dad remarried right away, and my young stepmom moved in.

324
00:22:06,983 --> 00:22:11,353
I was worried that as a teenager, I'd get in the way of the newlyweds,

325
00:22:12,253 --> 00:22:14,353
so I left home and have been drifting around ever since.

326
00:22:15,253 --> 00:22:18,853
Oh, gosh. You had to grow up way too fast.

327
00:22:26,133 --> 00:22:29,303
I have been so lonely and had such a hard time

328
00:22:29,573 --> 00:22:33,743
But it's only a rehearsal

329
00:22:35,443 --> 00:22:39,143
I'm not going to fall down

330
00:22:39,313 --> 00:22:42,113
I got this

331
00:22:49,083 --> 00:22:52,393
That song... It's my favourite.

332
00:22:52,923 --> 00:22:55,323
Really? Mine, too.

333
00:22:59,333 --> 00:23:02,703
Hey, what's your name?

334
00:23:03,803 --> 00:23:05,133
It's a secret.

335
00:23:17,913 --> 00:23:21,123
I have been so lonely and had such a hard time

336
00:23:21,623 --> 00:23:25,523
But it's only a rehearsal

337
00:23:27,093 --> 00:23:30,633
I'm not going to fall down

338
00:23:31,163 --> 00:23:34,303
I got this

339
00:23:34,403 --> 00:23:36,373
(Gong Ju Ah)

340
00:23:43,173 --> 00:23:44,643
Goodbye, Yang Hyun Bin.

341
00:23:45,113 --> 00:23:47,143
You have to find happiness, and then come back.

342
00:23:47,843 --> 00:23:48,843
Okay?

343
00:24:07,903 --> 00:24:11,303
Thanks to you, I tried my best to be happy.

344
00:24:12,603 --> 00:24:14,143
No wonder you looked so familiar.

345
00:24:16,673 --> 00:24:17,843
I'm back,

346
00:24:19,413 --> 00:24:20,413
Gong Ju Ah.

347
00:24:53,843 --> 00:24:55,543
Seong Mi, I wrote this for you.

348
00:24:56,313 --> 00:24:57,453
It's an original song.

349
00:25:04,253 --> 00:25:08,423
The clear tear welling in your eye

350
00:25:10,793 --> 00:25:14,533
Makes my heart rate spike

351
00:25:16,773 --> 00:25:18,773
Ba-dump, ba-dump

352
00:25:19,843 --> 00:25:24,043
You're my own IV fluid, my private intravenous shot

353
00:25:24,943 --> 00:25:29,413
You are my cure for arrhythmia

354
00:25:29,913 --> 00:25:34,383
You are my personal IV, my own Band-Aid

355
00:25:35,023 --> 00:25:39,353
You've completely healed all my wounds

356
00:25:41,663 --> 00:25:44,133
Give me a lifetime prescription

357
00:25:44,193 --> 00:25:47,633
With unlimited refills

358
00:25:51,273 --> 00:25:53,173
Good grief...

359
00:26:00,113 --> 00:26:04,553
I must have been out of my mind. My frontal lobe must've been frozen.

360
00:26:08,553 --> 00:26:09,553
Darn...

361
00:26:13,923 --> 00:26:15,023
What the...

362
00:26:16,963 --> 00:26:18,033
What was that?

363
00:27:14,383 --> 00:27:15,723
Please...

364
00:27:44,253 --> 00:27:45,353
You scared me!

365
00:27:46,183 --> 00:27:50,553
- Mom? I thought you went home. - Isn't this my house, too?

366
00:27:50,723 --> 00:27:54,463
Don't tell me you slept with Dad. In the same bed?

367
00:27:54,863 --> 00:27:57,793
- Unbelievable. - Don't change the subject.

368
00:27:58,593 --> 00:28:00,163
Where have you been all this time?

369
00:28:01,233 --> 00:28:03,133
Well, I...

370
00:28:03,403 --> 00:28:04,903
Gosh, you reek of alcohol.

371
00:28:09,743 --> 00:28:10,743
You.

372
00:28:11,473 --> 00:28:12,983
What are you wearing?

373
00:28:13,243 --> 00:28:17,613
- Wait. Isn't this a man's shirt? - No, it's not.

374
00:28:17,753 --> 00:28:18,953
No?

375
00:28:19,553 --> 00:28:20,653
Tell me the truth, right now!

376
00:28:20,723 --> 00:28:23,493
That hurt! What's your problem? Are you some kind of thug?

377
00:28:24,053 --> 00:28:26,723
And you call yourself a "love evangelist?"

378
00:28:26,793 --> 00:28:29,593
You're quitting your job. Right now.

379
00:28:29,963 --> 00:28:32,433
Leave your job and start training to become a specialist doctor.

380
00:28:33,303 --> 00:28:34,563
There you go again.

381
00:28:34,633 --> 00:28:38,733
You've fooled around long enough. You can't even do your job properly.

382
00:28:38,803 --> 00:28:41,143
Just quit before you humiliate yourself again.

383
00:28:41,203 --> 00:28:46,043
I bet you were praying I'd fail! Just waiting for me to mess up.

384
00:28:46,173 --> 00:28:50,083
When your daughter's struggling, shouldn't you be there for her?

385
00:28:50,083 --> 00:28:53,323
You're the one who messed up. Why are you taking it out on me?

386
00:28:53,983 --> 00:28:58,623
Projecting your anxiety and guilt. Psychoanalytically speaking...

387
00:28:58,623 --> 00:29:02,423
Just stop it! Why are you always analysing me?

388
00:29:02,493 --> 00:29:04,933
What, am I your patient? Unbelievable!

389
00:29:06,063 --> 00:29:09,203
Why do you always lock your door? To keep me out?

390
00:29:09,563 --> 00:29:11,103
To keep you out!

391
00:29:13,643 --> 00:29:14,643
The nerve.

392
00:29:39,063 --> 00:29:40,063
Hello.

393
00:29:40,363 --> 00:29:41,363
Hello.

394
00:29:41,633 --> 00:29:43,903
Right. The young lady left a while ago.

395
00:29:44,403 --> 00:29:45,833
She did?

396
00:29:48,273 --> 00:29:51,813
That's a shame. There's clam soup for breakfast.

397
00:29:53,483 --> 00:29:55,713
She should've had some. Her stomach's probably killing her.

398
00:29:59,613 --> 00:30:01,953
Oh, this is good.

399
00:30:03,153 --> 00:30:04,453
Hey, Ju Ah.

400
00:30:04,893 --> 00:30:07,623
So what's going to happen with work? Can you not go in starting tomorrow?

401
00:30:07,723 --> 00:30:11,663
How could she? That video of her is all over the Internet.

402
00:30:11,963 --> 00:30:15,833
People make mistakes. Why should this stop my work?

403
00:30:15,903 --> 00:30:18,133
That's right. You tell them, Ju Ah.

404
00:30:20,573 --> 00:30:21,573
Seong Mi.

405
00:30:22,203 --> 00:30:25,413
How about you end your lease and move back in?

406
00:30:25,913 --> 00:30:26,913
What?

407
00:30:27,883 --> 00:30:29,713
Dad, you made it so obvious that you hate the idea.

408
00:30:31,013 --> 00:30:32,413
Did I?

409
00:30:32,913 --> 00:30:34,923
I'm all for it. A hundred percent.

410
00:30:35,453 --> 00:30:37,723
I'm against it. Absolutely against it.

411
00:30:40,263 --> 00:30:42,363
Mother, why the sudden suggestion?

412
00:30:43,333 --> 00:30:45,693
You know what they say, "Out of sight, out of mind."

413
00:30:46,393 --> 00:30:48,203
I think all this divorce talk started...

414
00:30:48,203 --> 00:30:51,003
- What? Divorce? - because you two live apart.

415
00:30:51,333 --> 00:30:55,643
Even if you bicker, isn't it better under one roof?

416
00:30:55,973 --> 00:31:00,243
But Mother, I only moved because the commute was killing me.

417
00:31:00,983 --> 00:31:04,753
Besides, my lease isn't up yet, so it'd be hard to break it.

418
00:31:05,583 --> 00:31:09,453
- I can live in your place, Mom. - Be quiet.

419
00:31:09,853 --> 00:31:11,153
We'll think about it.

420
00:31:12,193 --> 00:31:14,293
What's there for you to think about?

421
00:31:15,893 --> 00:31:18,563
Right, Mom. Your show is on today, isn't it?

422
00:31:18,633 --> 00:31:20,063
That's right. Let's watch it.

423
00:31:20,403 --> 00:31:22,163
It's probably started already. Hand me the remote. The remote.

424
00:31:22,233 --> 00:31:26,203
Gosh, do we have to watch that? Her own family is a train wreck,

425
00:31:26,273 --> 00:31:29,773
- and she tells others how to live. - Gong Ju Ah.

426
00:31:30,173 --> 00:31:31,173
That's enough.

427
00:31:31,443 --> 00:31:32,443
Yes, ma'am.

428
00:31:35,043 --> 00:31:36,043
What?

429
00:31:38,853 --> 00:31:43,293
First, we respect each other, and we don't bottle up our emotions.

430
00:31:43,523 --> 00:31:48,123
We've learned to communicate without blaming each other.

431
00:31:49,023 --> 00:31:51,893
My, I bet every family in Korea is envious of you.

432
00:31:51,893 --> 00:31:54,633
You're such a perfect, exemplary family.

433
00:31:55,633 --> 00:31:58,103
What a joke. Gosh, I can't stand her.

434
00:32:00,503 --> 00:32:03,913
- Maybe I should expose them all. - Expose what?

435
00:32:04,313 --> 00:32:08,313
I'll say Dr. Han's father-in-law left his own family for our mom...

436
00:32:08,383 --> 00:32:10,983
and humiliate her so badly she can't show her face on TV again.

437
00:32:11,383 --> 00:32:14,623
Who would be embarrassed? Think about it.

438
00:32:15,123 --> 00:32:16,253
Oh, brother.

439
00:32:17,853 --> 00:32:18,853
Hey, Eun Bin.

440
00:32:19,823 --> 00:32:22,023
- Did you know? Your dad... - What about him?

441
00:32:22,293 --> 00:32:26,803
The woman my husband had a crush on married Dr. Gong, so he...

442
00:32:26,933 --> 00:32:28,763
married Eun Bin's mom on the rebound?

443
00:32:32,033 --> 00:32:35,973
The whole family knows. If you bring it up again,

444
00:32:36,043 --> 00:32:37,043
it'll be the thousandth time.

445
00:32:37,843 --> 00:32:38,913
Have I talked about it that much?

446
00:32:39,843 --> 00:32:43,583
Anyway, Han Seong Mi is still pretty.

447
00:32:43,653 --> 00:32:45,813
- Right, Dong Ik? - Pretty? What's pretty about her?

448
00:32:46,213 --> 00:32:47,853
She looks so old, I can barely recognise her.

449
00:32:49,683 --> 00:32:54,023
Are you blind? She looks incredible for her age.

450
00:32:54,223 --> 00:32:56,423
I get it. It's just sour grapes because she's out of your league.

451
00:32:57,993 --> 00:33:00,033
Are you out of your mind?

452
00:33:01,933 --> 00:33:06,843
I think Dr. Han Seong Mi is amazing. She's so classy and elegant.

453
00:33:06,903 --> 00:33:10,813
That must be why my dad liked her. Right, Stepmom?

454
00:33:11,843 --> 00:33:15,383
- I suppose so. - Can you all knock it off?

455
00:33:16,213 --> 00:33:19,553
What a way to start the morning. Why are we even talking about them?

456
00:33:20,653 --> 00:33:25,123
I hope my future mother-in-law is just like her. Wait.

457
00:33:25,193 --> 00:33:29,363
They have the perfect guy for me! Woo Jae!

458
00:33:29,423 --> 00:33:31,733
Hey! Don't you even joke about that.

459
00:33:31,793 --> 00:33:33,603
Do you want to give Grandfather a heart attack?

460
00:33:33,863 --> 00:33:36,633
And that's not all. Woo Jae's mom was Dad's first love.

461
00:33:36,873 --> 00:33:39,233
So? That's ancient history.

462
00:33:39,303 --> 00:33:42,543
Eun Bin, listen. You can have your pick of any man in the world,

463
00:33:42,603 --> 00:33:44,713
and I'll make sure you get whatever your heart desires, but...

464
00:33:45,473 --> 00:33:47,813
- not him. - What? Why not?

465
00:33:47,913 --> 00:33:49,183
Because...

466
00:33:50,513 --> 00:33:52,353
the thought of becoming in-laws with that woman...

467
00:33:52,613 --> 00:33:54,853
I don't have a single shred of interest in that.

468
00:34:40,633 --> 00:34:42,203
I'm thinking of growing it out.

469
00:34:42,203 --> 00:34:45,133
- You'd look pretty either way. - This is my hair without bangs.

470
00:34:47,403 --> 00:34:48,403
Right.

471
00:34:49,043 --> 00:34:50,573
It was dark. My eyes were playing tricks on me.

472
00:34:51,173 --> 00:34:52,573
And the angle was all wrong.

473
00:34:53,843 --> 00:34:57,283
- My darling would never do that. - Right.

474
00:34:57,713 --> 00:35:00,723
You scared me. Hey, I told you to act like you don't know me.

475
00:35:00,853 --> 00:35:03,593
Then don't stand in the middle of the street. Move.

476
00:35:05,953 --> 00:35:08,663
Ji Hu, you should greet your elders when you see them.

477
00:35:08,723 --> 00:35:10,333
But you just said to act like we don't know you.

478
00:35:12,293 --> 00:35:13,293
Hello, sir.

479
00:35:14,403 --> 00:35:15,663
You're a handsome kid.

480
00:35:16,063 --> 00:35:18,033
- Isn't he? - He must take after his dad.

481
00:35:20,003 --> 00:35:23,713
- Does he get good grades? - Of course. He's incredibly smart.

482
00:35:23,773 --> 00:35:25,273
Oh, that's strange.

483
00:35:25,813 --> 00:35:27,513
I didn't think you carried the smart gene.

484
00:35:29,583 --> 00:35:32,053
Then why is it you don't have any kids yet?

485
00:35:32,413 --> 00:35:35,323
Right. Is it too difficult at her age?

486
00:35:35,823 --> 00:35:39,123
It was better when you were married and gone. Why did you move back?

487
00:35:39,393 --> 00:35:41,463
Right, your husband blew all your money,

488
00:35:41,463 --> 00:35:42,863
so you're living with your family.

489
00:35:42,963 --> 00:35:44,963
I'm off. Wait.

490
00:35:45,033 --> 00:35:46,863
Dong Suk, I'm only asking because I'm genuinely curious.

491
00:35:47,563 --> 00:35:49,203
How much did he lose, exactly? See you.

492
00:35:50,473 --> 00:35:52,703
- Gosh, can you believe that guy? - Don't get mad.

493
00:35:53,503 --> 00:35:54,503
He's not wrong, though.

494
00:36:01,513 --> 00:36:03,383
(Gong Myeong Jeong Dae Han Clinic)

495
00:36:06,513 --> 00:36:08,483
(Sunny Korean Medicine Clinic)

496
00:36:10,453 --> 00:36:11,453
My gosh.

497
00:36:13,723 --> 00:36:15,123
(Gong Myeong Jeong Dae Han Clinic)

498
00:36:25,373 --> 00:36:26,373
Hello.

499
00:36:27,643 --> 00:36:29,543
Yes. Hello.

500
00:36:30,673 --> 00:36:32,913
Here. This is for you.

501
00:36:37,913 --> 00:36:39,753
Should I do it here?

502
00:36:40,753 --> 00:36:43,623
- Do what? - Didn't you want my autograph?

503
00:36:45,093 --> 00:36:46,153
No, that's not it.

504
00:36:46,423 --> 00:36:49,123
It's an invitation to our clinic's grand opening.

505
00:36:49,493 --> 00:36:50,493
I'm sorry?

506
00:36:52,363 --> 00:36:56,463
- Oh, I see. - Gosh, don't you know who I am?

507
00:36:56,933 --> 00:36:59,373
I'm the wife of the director of this clinic.

508
00:36:59,703 --> 00:37:00,943
Oh, no. Dr. Han.

509
00:37:01,203 --> 00:37:03,343
You have trouble recognising faces, don't you?

510
00:37:03,773 --> 00:37:06,413
Oh, right. Now, I remember who you are.

511
00:37:07,313 --> 00:37:09,383
You're Yang Dong Ik's second wife.

512
00:37:09,983 --> 00:37:12,983
Aren't you? My apologies.

513
00:37:13,453 --> 00:37:15,853
Your face has changed a bit. I didn't recognise you.

514
00:37:16,483 --> 00:37:18,293
You must've had some work done, right?

515
00:37:19,553 --> 00:37:20,663
No, I haven't.

516
00:37:21,293 --> 00:37:24,333
I think your eyes are getting old, Doctor.

517
00:37:24,763 --> 00:37:26,293
Then again, you are at that age, aren't you?

518
00:37:31,373 --> 00:37:33,433
Hey, Yang Dong Ik! Long time no see.

519
00:37:39,613 --> 00:37:41,043
I know you two were classmates,

520
00:37:41,513 --> 00:37:43,853
but he has a certain social standing and reputation now.

521
00:37:44,113 --> 00:37:46,413
Calling him just by his full name...

522
00:37:46,753 --> 00:37:48,953
is hardly appropriate, don't you think?

523
00:37:49,923 --> 00:37:50,923
Really?

524
00:37:51,353 --> 00:37:54,523
Back in college, we used to call him Bucket.

525
00:37:56,323 --> 00:37:57,333
Bucket.

526
00:37:58,033 --> 00:37:59,133
Bucket!

527
00:37:59,693 --> 00:38:03,103
My, Doctor, you're so mischievous.

528
00:38:07,943 --> 00:38:08,943
Was I?

529
00:38:12,143 --> 00:38:13,143
Well, then...

530
00:38:16,113 --> 00:38:17,383
Gosh, how conceited.

531
00:38:18,553 --> 00:38:20,013
(Gong Myeong Jeong Dae Han Clinic)

532
00:38:20,013 --> 00:38:21,023
I heard that.

533
00:38:23,223 --> 00:38:25,753
I meant for you to hear me.

534
00:38:30,393 --> 00:38:34,703
(Gong Myeong Jeong Dae Han Clinic)

535
00:38:35,033 --> 00:38:37,803
I swear I'm going to run her out of this town.

536
00:38:40,543 --> 00:38:42,443
What? Where did he go?

537
00:38:50,083 --> 00:38:51,083
Hello?

538
00:38:54,783 --> 00:38:56,753
What? Who?

539
00:38:58,723 --> 00:39:01,293
Looks like Bucket's wife is jealous of you.

540
00:39:01,893 --> 00:39:04,593
Well, it's a classic case of transference.

541
00:39:04,933 --> 00:39:06,863
A competitive anxiety response, I'd say.

542
00:39:09,233 --> 00:39:10,233
Hey, so...

543
00:39:10,573 --> 00:39:12,833
Why did you stop by the clinic? Did you have something to tell me?

544
00:39:14,773 --> 00:39:15,773
Yes.

545
00:39:16,203 --> 00:39:17,213
What is it?

546
00:39:17,943 --> 00:39:19,543
About not wanting to move back here?

547
00:39:20,483 --> 00:39:22,813
The commute is just brutal.

548
00:39:23,313 --> 00:39:26,713
And honestly, you must've felt it too.

549
00:39:27,353 --> 00:39:29,623
After living apart for over three years,

550
00:39:29,923 --> 00:39:32,053
it's awkward sleeping together, you know.

551
00:39:32,623 --> 00:39:34,223
I couldn't even sleep properly last night.

552
00:39:35,823 --> 00:39:38,563
Okay, I'll talk to my mom about it.

553
00:39:39,593 --> 00:39:40,963
And...

554
00:39:42,163 --> 00:39:45,233
I'm sorry about bringing up divorce.

555
00:39:45,933 --> 00:39:47,173
I was out of line yesterday.

556
00:39:48,673 --> 00:39:52,373
I know what it's like to feel that loss and helplessness.

557
00:39:54,443 --> 00:39:55,713
I'm sorry, too.

558
00:39:58,053 --> 00:40:00,923
Well, look at that. The great Han Seong Mi, apologising.

559
00:40:01,523 --> 00:40:04,493
Please, let's just focus on our family for a change.

560
00:40:04,953 --> 00:40:07,193
Stop worrying about everyone else for once, okay?

561
00:40:07,823 --> 00:40:09,693
Hey, but back in the day,

562
00:40:10,393 --> 00:40:12,933
isn't that why you fell for me in the first place?

563
00:40:13,593 --> 00:40:15,933
Please. Don't even bring up the past.

564
00:40:16,503 --> 00:40:18,233
I'm the one who dug my own grave.

565
00:40:20,803 --> 00:40:22,003
You dug your own grave?

566
00:40:39,293 --> 00:40:40,523
Beautiful lady.

567
00:40:41,063 --> 00:40:42,293
May I join you?

568
00:40:44,663 --> 00:40:45,663
Oh, my.

569
00:40:47,733 --> 00:40:48,733
My goodness.

570
00:40:50,403 --> 00:40:53,073
It's even better to see you than I'd imagined.

571
00:40:56,073 --> 00:40:58,373
Gosh, can I...

572
00:40:59,513 --> 00:41:01,843
Can I just give you a hug?

573
00:41:14,493 --> 00:41:15,493
Why isn't she here yet?

574
00:41:16,793 --> 00:41:17,793
Where did she run off to?

575
00:41:20,333 --> 00:41:21,333
(Seoul)

576
00:41:22,063 --> 00:41:23,163
(Wifey)

577
00:41:23,633 --> 00:41:25,973
What? When did she go to Seoul?

578
00:41:27,373 --> 00:41:29,843
What? A hotel?

579
00:41:34,813 --> 00:41:37,613
You've become even more handsome. So masculine.

580
00:41:38,383 --> 00:41:41,553
Wow, Se Ri. You haven't changed a bit.

581
00:41:41,923 --> 00:41:43,523
Anyone would believe you're my girlfriend.

582
00:41:45,123 --> 00:41:47,393
You know I'm deadly serious about my upkeep.

583
00:41:47,763 --> 00:41:52,033
For us former beauty queens, our looks are everything.

584
00:41:59,233 --> 00:42:01,573
- How is everyone doing? - Good.

585
00:42:02,173 --> 00:42:04,813
Speak of the devil.

586
00:42:05,443 --> 00:42:06,913
Is that my dad? Here, let me get it.

587
00:42:11,313 --> 00:42:13,383
- Hello? - Who is this?

588
00:42:15,923 --> 00:42:17,253
Don't you recognise my voice?

589
00:42:17,593 --> 00:42:19,193
I don't. Who is this, you punk?

590
00:42:19,523 --> 00:42:21,493
What kind of scumbag are you to be in a hotel with my wife?

591
00:42:22,493 --> 00:42:24,363
What? How did he know we're at a hotel?

592
00:42:24,833 --> 00:42:26,593
Wait, don't tell me you're tracking her location.

593
00:42:26,793 --> 00:42:29,203
That's right, you punk. You're so busted.

594
00:42:29,333 --> 00:42:32,803
Don't you move a muscle. I'm heading over there now. Got it?

595
00:42:36,573 --> 00:42:37,613
It's me, Dad.

596
00:42:39,673 --> 00:42:41,213
Why, you little...

597
00:42:41,783 --> 00:42:44,083
Hey! If you were back in town, you punk,

598
00:42:44,653 --> 00:42:46,353
you should have called me first.

599
00:42:47,683 --> 00:42:50,053
Now, you know who the "other guy" is. Are we good?

600
00:42:50,323 --> 00:42:54,093
Why would you track her? Seriously, stop. I'm hanging up.

601
00:42:54,163 --> 00:42:55,763
Hey, Hyun Bin! Hey, Yang Hyun Bin!

602
00:42:59,663 --> 00:43:00,663
Thank you.

603
00:43:01,203 --> 00:43:02,933
For putting up with a man like my father.

604
00:43:04,403 --> 00:43:07,443
Putting up with him? I'm truly happy.

605
00:43:09,373 --> 00:43:12,013
Doesn't it bother you that my dad is so suspicious?

606
00:43:13,913 --> 00:43:17,143
I see it as his way of showing he cares.

607
00:43:18,613 --> 00:43:20,113
Do you really love my father that much?

608
00:43:23,483 --> 00:43:24,553
I...

609
00:43:25,893 --> 00:43:26,993
I understand him.

610
00:43:27,723 --> 00:43:29,063
He's been through a lot, you know.

611
00:43:30,263 --> 00:43:32,693
His mother left home over an affair,

612
00:43:33,393 --> 00:43:35,933
and his wife cheated on him as well.

613
00:43:39,973 --> 00:43:40,973
I...

614
00:43:42,203 --> 00:43:44,873
I think my grandfather and my dad were the ones at fault.

615
00:43:45,613 --> 00:43:48,743
I believe that's why they both left. So...

616
00:43:49,483 --> 00:43:52,213
that's why I can't stand my grandfather or my dad.

617
00:43:53,453 --> 00:43:56,583
So is that why you left home? Afraid you'd end up like them?

618
00:43:58,193 --> 00:43:59,293
You're sharp.

619
00:44:02,963 --> 00:44:05,333
So, are you back for good?

620
00:44:05,763 --> 00:44:06,863
No, just for a year.

621
00:44:07,333 --> 00:44:10,103
An old classmate from Argentina asked me to help her with a project.

622
00:44:11,473 --> 00:44:12,473
"Her?" So, a girl?

623
00:44:13,773 --> 00:44:14,773
Yes.

624
00:44:16,303 --> 00:44:17,743
This should be interesting.

625
00:44:23,913 --> 00:44:25,883
(Taehan)

626
00:44:31,453 --> 00:44:35,493
Remember Manager Kang Min from our last collaboration?

627
00:44:36,363 --> 00:44:39,493
He's building a new brand's team, so I put in a good word for you all.

628
00:44:39,963 --> 00:44:43,263
So, everyone, please email him your resumes and portfolios.

629
00:44:43,863 --> 00:44:45,203
Thanks, boss.

630
00:44:47,203 --> 00:44:50,573
I'm sorry I couldn't stay with you guys until the end.

631
00:44:51,243 --> 00:44:53,413
Don't say that. We share the responsibility.

632
00:44:53,813 --> 00:44:55,813
We should have done one last quality check.

633
00:44:56,643 --> 00:44:59,983
It's awful that you're the only one whose career is getting tarnished.

634
00:45:01,983 --> 00:45:02,983
Oh, well...

635
00:45:10,193 --> 00:45:11,733
But doesn't it seem really weird?

636
00:45:12,433 --> 00:45:15,163
We ran QC on samples over three times.

637
00:45:15,163 --> 00:45:16,803
There were no issues at the fitting.

638
00:45:17,333 --> 00:45:20,133
The sourcing team confirmed the sewing and technical guidelines,

639
00:45:20,533 --> 00:45:22,303
and none of the secondary materials were defective.

640
00:45:22,573 --> 00:45:25,173
Exactly. You even tried it on the day before...

641
00:45:25,373 --> 00:45:27,683
and checked the zipper and all the other parts yourself.

642
00:45:38,693 --> 00:45:39,693
Oh, my.

643
00:45:40,293 --> 00:45:43,063
So, let me get this straight. You looked like death warmed over,

644
00:45:43,163 --> 00:45:46,663
went completely off-grid, and made me worry sick,

645
00:45:47,163 --> 00:45:50,003
only to cuddle up and sleep with a total stranger?

646
00:45:50,133 --> 00:45:52,973
Yes, I was dying to brag to you about it.

647
00:45:53,173 --> 00:45:57,943
I bet it was nice to be in his arms after working yourself to death.

648
00:45:58,243 --> 00:46:00,543
See? You get me.

649
00:46:01,413 --> 00:46:02,843
And thanks for the life-saving chicken feet!

650
00:46:08,523 --> 00:46:11,193
I should be thanking you. For agreeing to go back to work.

651
00:46:11,523 --> 00:46:12,853
I really thought you were going to quit.

652
00:46:13,493 --> 00:46:14,493
Tell me about it.

653
00:46:15,893 --> 00:46:19,433
But the kindness of a stranger really gave me strength.

654
00:46:19,593 --> 00:46:22,533
Goodness. Are you going to see him again?

655
00:46:22,803 --> 00:46:25,333
What? How could I? I don't have his number.

656
00:46:26,273 --> 00:46:29,343
I don't even know his first name, or his last.

657
00:46:29,403 --> 00:46:30,713
I don't know a thing about him.

658
00:46:31,043 --> 00:46:32,973
You should've at least gotten his number.

659
00:46:34,283 --> 00:46:36,183
The moment was just so perfect on its own.

660
00:46:36,913 --> 00:46:40,483
I feel like seeing him again would somehow ruin it, you know?

661
00:46:41,453 --> 00:46:45,223
- If it's meant to be, we'll meet. - For crying out loud.

662
00:46:49,593 --> 00:46:50,593
Nice.

663
00:46:52,493 --> 00:46:53,763
Man...

664
00:46:54,933 --> 00:46:59,033
Wait, if Hyun Bin is back in Korea, why is he in a hotel and not home?

665
00:46:59,773 --> 00:47:02,873
He's the eldest son, yet he does whatever he wants.

666
00:47:04,873 --> 00:47:06,773
Does he really hate the sight of me that much?

667
00:47:07,273 --> 00:47:10,953
No, Father. He just chose a place close to the office.

668
00:47:11,653 --> 00:47:15,823
He said he's getting a studio soon. I told him to come and say hello.

669
00:47:17,453 --> 00:47:19,753
Didn't you tell him to do that?

670
00:47:19,753 --> 00:47:20,993
Because you don't want him to live with us?

671
00:47:21,363 --> 00:47:25,463
Grandfather, let's be honest. He went abroad because of her.

672
00:47:26,793 --> 00:47:27,803
Get out.

673
00:47:30,303 --> 00:47:32,603
Goodness. What is going on in there?

674
00:47:33,073 --> 00:47:36,143
- Why can't I hear anything? - What are you doing? I'm hungry.

675
00:47:36,403 --> 00:47:39,273
Is food all you can think about? Hyun Bin is back.

676
00:47:39,643 --> 00:47:41,413
If Hyun Bin moves back in, we'll have to give up our room.

677
00:47:41,843 --> 00:47:44,453
- So, we're getting kicked out? - Well...

678
00:47:44,753 --> 00:47:45,753
What are you two doing here?

679
00:47:47,753 --> 00:47:50,383
Is Hyun Bin really moving in?

680
00:47:53,853 --> 00:47:55,823
No, he's getting his own place.

681
00:47:58,333 --> 00:47:59,993
Thank goodness.

682
00:48:02,533 --> 00:48:04,633
He said he'll be in Korea for one year.

683
00:48:05,003 --> 00:48:07,703
I'll use this year to make amends and make sure he never leaves again.

684
00:48:08,203 --> 00:48:10,843
Don't you worry, Father. Just leave everything to me.

685
00:48:12,943 --> 00:48:15,743
Do as you see fit, Se Ri. I trust you.

686
00:48:16,883 --> 00:48:19,353
What are you planning?

687
00:48:20,753 --> 00:48:21,853
As for our Hyun Bin,

688
00:48:23,253 --> 00:48:24,253
I plan on getting him married.

689
00:48:47,273 --> 00:48:49,583
What is wrong with me?

690
00:48:55,823 --> 00:48:58,523
You're fine.

691
00:48:59,253 --> 00:49:02,923
You're fine. You can do this! I'm so sorry.

692
00:49:04,263 --> 00:49:05,863
- What? - What?

693
00:49:05,963 --> 00:49:08,203
- What are you doing here? - I could ask you the same thing.

694
00:49:08,333 --> 00:49:09,903
Wait, are you here to see me?

695
00:49:10,163 --> 00:49:12,433
- Of course not. - Then why?

696
00:49:13,073 --> 00:49:15,473
- It must be a coincidence. - There's no way.

697
00:49:16,073 --> 00:49:17,373
If not a coincidence, then what?

698
00:49:17,913 --> 00:49:21,513
Don't tell me you got the wrong idea about me from the other night.

699
00:49:22,013 --> 00:49:23,013
What?

700
00:49:23,013 --> 00:49:27,383
Is this all because we fell asleep holding each other?

701
00:49:27,653 --> 00:49:29,783
What? We slept in each other's arms?

702
00:49:30,153 --> 00:49:33,523
No. Nothing like that ever happened.

703
00:49:34,153 --> 00:49:38,763
Then this must be a coincidence. And this is where it ends.

704
00:49:38,763 --> 00:49:40,933
Got it? Don't follow me.

705
00:50:00,383 --> 00:50:01,423
What is with this guy?

706
00:50:02,683 --> 00:50:03,723
Security! Over here!

707
00:50:04,723 --> 00:50:05,993
Please stop that man!

708
00:50:07,553 --> 00:50:08,563
Seriously?

709
00:50:09,393 --> 00:50:10,393
Unbelievable.

710
00:50:11,563 --> 00:50:13,793
Excuse me, Ms. Gong Ju Ah, let me explain.

711
00:50:14,233 --> 00:50:17,873
How do you know my name? You saw that video of me!

712
00:50:18,333 --> 00:50:20,833
- He's a stalker! A stalker! - Come on.

713
00:50:21,043 --> 00:50:24,273
- Seriously. - No! I'm not a stalker.

714
00:50:24,413 --> 00:50:27,473
- Sir, please calm down and listen. - What's going on?

715
00:50:27,473 --> 00:50:28,583
I'm not a stalker.

716
00:50:31,683 --> 00:50:33,813
What's wrong? Who is this guy?

717
00:50:34,623 --> 00:50:39,393
- Let's just go. Come on. Seriously. - Excuse me! Can we just talk?

718
00:50:39,823 --> 00:50:42,523
I'm really not a stalker. Look.

719
00:50:42,523 --> 00:50:43,763
I start working here today...

720
00:50:43,763 --> 00:50:44,833
Pacu Nacho?

721
00:50:49,303 --> 00:50:52,603
Hye Su. Help me out here.

722
00:50:53,933 --> 00:50:55,743
Let him go. He's an employee.

723
00:51:00,913 --> 00:51:03,243
You finally made it, Pacu Nacho.

724
00:51:04,353 --> 00:51:06,583
I know, right? How long has it been?

725
00:51:17,763 --> 00:51:19,563
That's the guy you slept with?

726
00:51:23,433 --> 00:51:24,433
Sorry.

727
00:51:25,673 --> 00:51:26,733
Hold on.

728
00:51:27,373 --> 00:51:29,603
Didn't you say you didn't have his number or anything?

729
00:51:30,403 --> 00:51:32,073
Did you happen to mention where you work or something?

730
00:51:32,643 --> 00:51:34,313
I think he saw the home shopping video.

731
00:51:36,783 --> 00:51:39,513
This is a big deal.

732
00:51:42,883 --> 00:51:45,123
(Taehan Home Shopping Special)

733
00:51:45,193 --> 00:51:48,023
Was this really a mistake?

734
00:51:48,563 --> 00:51:50,123
Don't you think we should look into this?

735
00:51:50,593 --> 00:51:51,593
You handle it.

736
00:51:52,333 --> 00:51:54,293
Let's sort out your work schedule first.

737
00:51:54,863 --> 00:51:56,363
We're in a really bad spot right now.

738
00:51:56,803 --> 00:51:59,403
We're losing our competitive edge to imported brands.

739
00:51:59,673 --> 00:52:00,803
That's why I'm here.

740
00:52:01,273 --> 00:52:03,643
With an instinct for branding that anticipates trends...

741
00:52:04,073 --> 00:52:07,173
and a reputation for one-of-a-kind marketing,

742
00:52:07,783 --> 00:52:08,983
Pacu Nacho Yang.

743
00:52:09,383 --> 00:52:10,713
I'm so grateful.

744
00:52:11,283 --> 00:52:12,953
Thanks for answering my S.O.S. on such short notice.

745
00:52:13,253 --> 00:52:15,753
When I was broke back in Argentina,

746
00:52:15,823 --> 00:52:18,623
you always bought me food and helped me get through school.

747
00:52:18,893 --> 00:52:21,623
- Of course, I have to repay you. - I guess the meals really paid off.

748
00:52:22,193 --> 00:52:24,323
- You start tomorrow? - Sure. Why not?

749
00:52:25,193 --> 00:52:26,263
Wait.

750
00:52:27,063 --> 00:52:30,663
As head of the fashion division, do I have hiring and firing power?

751
00:52:31,703 --> 00:52:32,703
Unbelievable.

752
00:52:37,743 --> 00:52:40,073
I went back to the lobby, but that jerk was gone.

753
00:52:40,573 --> 00:52:41,583
My gosh.

754
00:52:42,183 --> 00:52:43,783
Isn't it weird, though?

755
00:52:44,143 --> 00:52:47,683
Once a guy falls for me, he'll stop at nothing.

756
00:52:47,783 --> 00:52:51,123
Hey. Enough with the unconfirmed stories.

757
00:52:51,623 --> 00:52:53,293
And get going. The vice president's asking for you.

758
00:52:54,223 --> 00:52:55,463
The vice president?

759
00:52:57,023 --> 00:52:58,433
After an internal review,

760
00:52:58,993 --> 00:53:01,163
regarding the recent home shopping broadcast incident,

761
00:53:01,763 --> 00:53:05,803
we've decided to ask for your resignation, Ms. Gong.

762
00:53:07,233 --> 00:53:11,643
I thought the penalty for losing was a demotion.

763
00:53:11,913 --> 00:53:16,243
That only applies if you fall behind in a performance review.

764
00:53:17,013 --> 00:53:20,483
This incident not only damaged our brand's public image,

765
00:53:20,553 --> 00:53:23,283
but it also undermined the trust in our quality control.

766
00:53:23,783 --> 00:53:27,553
I'm sorry. I have no excuse for that.

767
00:53:28,563 --> 00:53:29,563
But...

768
00:53:29,993 --> 00:53:33,233
even if I have to quit, please let me investigate this.

769
00:53:34,433 --> 00:53:35,433
An investigation?

770
00:53:35,763 --> 00:53:39,673
I believe that someone intentionally interfered with this.

771
00:53:40,273 --> 00:53:42,473
I want to be the one to uncover the truth.

772
00:53:43,073 --> 00:53:44,473
I can't just leave like this.

773
00:53:46,813 --> 00:53:48,113
Someone once told me...

774
00:53:49,113 --> 00:53:50,113
that I...

775
00:53:50,943 --> 00:53:52,653
am someone who creates happiness.

776
00:53:54,723 --> 00:53:59,153
I want people to feel happy when they wear the clothes I design.

777
00:54:00,123 --> 00:54:02,763
I don't want to leave in disgrace like this.

778
00:54:03,323 --> 00:54:04,323
Please.

779
00:54:12,673 --> 00:54:14,973
You'll work under the new executive director.

780
00:54:17,973 --> 00:54:19,743
Yes. Of course.

781
00:54:19,973 --> 00:54:24,413
But isn't he a foreigner? I'm not sure if I can...

782
00:54:24,483 --> 00:54:27,553
- communicate with him... - Make an effort.

783
00:54:28,623 --> 00:54:31,123
I'm waiving disciplinary action, so it's the least you can do.

784
00:54:31,853 --> 00:54:35,763
Yes, I'll do my best. Thank you, Vice President.

785
00:54:37,293 --> 00:54:38,293
Well, then...

786
00:54:40,533 --> 00:54:41,663
But, Vice President...

787
00:54:43,463 --> 00:54:46,473
Be careful. There's a lunatic in the lobby.

788
00:54:47,773 --> 00:54:48,773
What?

789
00:54:49,143 --> 00:54:50,203
You see,

790
00:54:50,443 --> 00:54:53,543
I happened to run into him a couple of days ago.

791
00:54:53,713 --> 00:54:56,143
But I never thought he'd follow me all the way to the office.

792
00:54:56,813 --> 00:54:58,853
He must be some unhinged stalker.

793
00:55:00,453 --> 00:55:03,023
I just thought you should be aware.

794
00:55:04,253 --> 00:55:05,253
I'll be on my way.

795
00:55:08,823 --> 00:55:10,823
(Taehan Group)

796
00:55:22,603 --> 00:55:24,073
What's going on, Pacu Nacho?

797
00:55:25,073 --> 00:55:26,373
(Taehan Group)

798
00:55:26,443 --> 00:55:28,113
What was that about with Gong Ju Ah?

799
00:55:31,653 --> 00:55:33,853
I'm kind of excited.

800
00:55:34,383 --> 00:55:35,653
About life at this company.

801
00:55:38,993 --> 00:55:41,363
(President of the Association of Korean Medicine)

802
00:55:41,423 --> 00:55:44,863
Our Sunny Korean Medicine Clinic has been completely renovated!

803
00:55:44,933 --> 00:55:47,463
Please take one. Both our treatments and our service...

804
00:55:47,533 --> 00:55:50,903
are on a whole new level of class. Please come visit!

805
00:55:50,963 --> 00:55:54,673
Right! Visit for a free consultation and enjoy a warm welcome tea.

806
00:55:54,743 --> 00:55:55,943
Here, take one.

807
00:55:56,373 --> 00:56:00,413
Stop by. We'll provide service that's in a class of its own.

808
00:56:00,673 --> 00:56:01,713
Excuse me, sir.

809
00:56:04,883 --> 00:56:07,213
(Sunny Korean Medicine Clinic)

810
00:56:07,213 --> 00:56:08,983
Where's Eun Bin? Why isn't she out here helping?

811
00:56:09,483 --> 00:56:11,223
She's inside, filming a vlog.

812
00:56:12,023 --> 00:56:13,193
She's so annoying.

813
00:56:13,523 --> 00:56:15,563
How will we get any customers like this?

814
00:56:16,023 --> 00:56:19,733
- Just wait. I've planned it all. - Planned what?

815
00:56:23,263 --> 00:56:24,673
Here she comes.

816
00:56:27,873 --> 00:56:28,903
What's this?

817
00:56:30,003 --> 00:56:34,783
Hey, everyone! It's Yanggaeng, from Sunny TV.

818
00:56:35,043 --> 00:56:38,513
You know that place that's a big hit with the moms in Onjeong right now?

819
00:56:38,783 --> 00:56:40,253
The holy grail of Korean medicine,

820
00:56:40,253 --> 00:56:42,883
Sunny Korean Medicine Clinic, has been renovated,

821
00:56:42,953 --> 00:56:44,693
so I had to come to check it out myself.

822
00:56:44,753 --> 00:56:46,053
(Sunny Korean Medicine Clinic)

823
00:56:46,123 --> 00:56:47,893
How luxurious!

824
00:56:48,563 --> 00:56:50,363
It's like a hotel lounge, isn't it?

825
00:56:52,133 --> 00:56:56,063
This is the star of our clinic,

826
00:56:56,203 --> 00:56:58,333
Director Yang Seon Chul.

827
00:56:58,703 --> 00:57:02,843
He's a specialist in chronic illness and can diagnose you by your pulse.

828
00:57:03,803 --> 00:57:05,273
Say a few words for us, Director.

829
00:57:05,943 --> 00:57:07,113
Get out.

830
00:57:12,483 --> 00:57:14,583
Yes! Looks like a chicken dinner for me tonight.

831
00:57:15,153 --> 00:57:18,023
- Why won't you die, stupid thing? - Ta-da!

832
00:57:19,193 --> 00:57:21,363
Next, our specialist for skin...

833
00:57:21,363 --> 00:57:23,523
and weight management for VIP clients...

834
00:57:23,593 --> 00:57:27,963
is Director Yang Dong Ik. Director, what's your signature treatment?

835
00:57:28,433 --> 00:57:31,773
It brightens skin, clears blemishes, and reduces wrinkles all at once.

836
00:57:31,833 --> 00:57:33,733
It's our Multi-Skin Youth-Restoring Acupuncture.

837
00:57:35,273 --> 00:57:38,643
See my firm, radiant skin? The secret to my complexion is...

838
00:57:38,713 --> 00:57:43,613
his signature treatment! This is Yanggaeng, signing off.

839
00:57:46,683 --> 00:57:50,283
Gosh, that was exhausting. Dad, you'd better pay me for this.

840
00:57:50,353 --> 00:57:51,693
Ten dollars per like.

841
00:57:52,293 --> 00:57:55,993
- Hey, are there any customers? - No. They're across the street.

842
00:57:56,323 --> 00:57:58,563
- Why? - I don't know. A flea market maybe?

843
00:57:58,563 --> 00:57:59,633
It's packed.

844
00:58:00,863 --> 00:58:02,503
Why today, of all days?

845
00:58:04,103 --> 00:58:05,203
Unbelievable.

846
00:58:07,233 --> 00:58:10,743
Everyone, Sang Gu's mother is closing her long-running store,

847
00:58:10,903 --> 00:58:15,013
so everything's on a huge discount. Come and take a look for yourself.

848
00:58:16,713 --> 00:58:18,883
This way, my patients can buy things on their way in and out.

849
00:58:19,313 --> 00:58:21,253
So just leave everything here until it's all sold out.

850
00:58:21,823 --> 00:58:25,823
Thank you so much. I was about to sell it all for next to nothing.

851
00:58:26,553 --> 00:58:28,293
After running the shop for over 30 years,

852
00:58:28,963 --> 00:58:30,123
it must be so hard to let it go.

853
00:58:30,763 --> 00:58:33,363
They suddenly hiked the rent by 500 dollars.

854
00:58:34,493 --> 00:58:35,733
What choice did I have?

855
00:58:35,963 --> 00:58:39,233
I don't know what's with everyone, suddenly raising all the rents.

856
00:58:39,473 --> 00:58:41,843
Tell me about it. The bedding store is for sale, too.

857
00:58:41,903 --> 00:58:44,673
- The head merchant is selling up. - Really?

858
00:58:46,313 --> 00:58:48,683
What's all that noise?

859
00:58:49,013 --> 00:58:51,553
It's the grand reopening for that other clinic today.

860
00:58:51,653 --> 00:58:55,053
Seriously, talk about not being able to read the room.

861
00:58:55,123 --> 00:58:56,423
- Hey, come on. - Take it easy.

862
00:58:56,483 --> 00:58:58,623
- Just stay out of it. - Let it go.

863
00:58:59,253 --> 00:59:00,393
I'll handle it.

864
00:59:00,453 --> 00:59:02,493
(Nurse Oh Jin Ah)

865
00:59:02,563 --> 00:59:05,093
- Thank you. - Sunny Korean Medicine Clinic!

866
00:59:05,093 --> 00:59:06,693
Yes. We recently renovated.

867
00:59:06,833 --> 00:59:09,633
Sunny Korean Medicine Clinic has been newly renovated! Here.

868
00:59:09,963 --> 00:59:11,003
- Right over here. - Sunny Korean Medicine Clinic.

869
00:59:11,063 --> 00:59:12,533
- Sunny Korean Medicine Clinic. - Thank you.

870
00:59:12,773 --> 00:59:14,603
- Thank you. - Thank you.

871
00:59:14,673 --> 00:59:15,673
Welcome to Sunny Korean Medicine Clinic.

872
00:59:16,443 --> 00:59:19,543
- Thank you. Please take one. - Sunny Korean Medicine Clinic!

873
00:59:19,813 --> 00:59:22,513
We've newly renovated. Please take one.

874
00:59:26,353 --> 00:59:29,423
Excuse me. We received a noise complaint,

875
00:59:29,483 --> 00:59:30,683
so we were dispatched to the scene.

876
00:59:32,093 --> 00:59:33,493
A noise complaint?

877
00:59:33,893 --> 00:59:36,193
This isn't a residential area. It's a market.

878
00:59:36,263 --> 00:59:38,863
Even in a market, we must enforce the rules if there is a complaint.

879
00:59:39,263 --> 00:59:43,003
The daytime limit is 70 decibels. You need to stay below that.

880
00:59:44,103 --> 00:59:45,433
See? You're over the limit.

881
00:59:46,733 --> 00:59:48,403
Who on earth would report something like this?

882
00:59:49,303 --> 00:59:52,743
I can't disclose who reported this. Their identity is protected.

883
00:59:53,443 --> 00:59:55,143
I don't need you to tell me. I know exactly who it was.

884
00:59:56,143 --> 00:59:57,513
(Gong Myeong Jeong Dae Han Clinic)

885
00:59:58,983 --> 01:00:01,853
Gosh, it's cold.

886
01:00:02,183 --> 01:00:03,183
All right.

887
01:00:03,723 --> 01:00:06,323
We'll turn the music off. Please turn it off.

888
01:00:07,053 --> 01:00:08,993
Thank you for your cooperation. I'll be on my way.

889
01:00:09,063 --> 01:00:10,723
Why are you turning off the music? Who gave you the right?

890
01:00:11,493 --> 01:00:12,633
Hurry up and turn it back on.

891
01:00:13,533 --> 01:00:17,063
Officer, that clinic over there is openly selling merchandise.

892
01:00:17,563 --> 01:00:20,273
If they're making untaxed profit, isn't that tax evasion?

893
01:00:21,033 --> 01:00:24,703
For tax evasion, call the tax office at 126. That's not my jurisdiction.

894
01:00:25,573 --> 01:00:28,983
Let it go, Director. We knew this was going to happen.

895
01:00:29,443 --> 01:00:31,983
This will all be over in a few days, so let's just be patient, okay?

896
01:00:32,783 --> 01:00:34,013
You might as well just sell your clinic.

897
01:00:35,923 --> 01:00:38,523
(Gong Myeong Jeong Dae Han Clinic, Pharmacy)

898
01:00:39,293 --> 01:00:41,963
- Mom, let's call it a day. - Just a second. I'm on the phone.

899
01:00:44,293 --> 01:00:45,393
Yes.

900
01:00:45,893 --> 01:00:48,703
Let me talk it over with my kids first.

901
01:00:49,703 --> 01:00:50,703
Okay.

902
01:00:51,833 --> 01:00:53,433
What is it? What's going on?

903
01:00:54,603 --> 01:00:57,803
He's asking us for more rent, too.

904
01:01:00,343 --> 01:01:01,473
Unbelievable.

905
01:01:02,483 --> 01:01:06,613
A 20 percent increase? You know we can't afford that.

906
01:01:06,883 --> 01:01:08,423
I'm very sorry, ma'am.

907
01:01:08,823 --> 01:01:11,423
Sir, would you care to explain?

908
01:01:11,723 --> 01:01:13,653
What in the world is going on here?

909
01:01:14,893 --> 01:01:15,993
The thing is...

910
01:01:16,593 --> 01:01:19,133
The landlords all had a meeting recently.

911
01:01:22,733 --> 01:01:27,033
So, to make the market look better, you want to get rid of old shops...

912
01:01:27,103 --> 01:01:29,343
and replace them all with franchises?

913
01:01:30,473 --> 01:01:31,873
I'm not saying we get rid of them,

914
01:01:32,043 --> 01:01:36,913
- but to switch to a stable model. - But listen.

915
01:01:37,213 --> 01:01:38,883
Hasn't business been good lately?

916
01:01:39,353 --> 01:01:41,983
The new apartment complex has brought in more people,

917
01:01:42,323 --> 01:01:43,853
and none of the tenants are behind on rent.

918
01:01:44,883 --> 01:01:46,823
That's just a flash in the pan, all right?

919
01:01:47,193 --> 01:01:50,223
Young people these days don't come to the market to shop.

920
01:01:50,493 --> 01:01:53,733
They buy everything on their phones. Isn't that right?

921
01:01:54,933 --> 01:01:58,733
You're familiar with Gopyeong Market in Sodang City, right?

922
01:01:59,403 --> 01:02:03,903
They partnered with Soban Company and franchised the entire market,

923
01:02:04,243 --> 01:02:05,313
and their sales...

924
01:02:06,113 --> 01:02:07,673
increased tenfold.

925
01:02:08,413 --> 01:02:12,953
Right, I saw that on the news. They sell 10,000 donuts a day,

926
01:02:13,153 --> 01:02:15,453
and they're making 5,000 dollars a day.

927
01:02:15,753 --> 01:02:18,523
But the shop owners here...

928
01:02:18,793 --> 01:02:22,463
have been in the same spot for 20 or 30 years.

929
01:02:24,423 --> 01:02:26,193
Do you really think they'll cooperate?

930
01:02:27,463 --> 01:02:28,933
If they won't leave,

931
01:02:29,903 --> 01:02:33,733
- we make them leave. - Come on. You think it's that easy?

932
01:02:34,133 --> 01:02:36,573
Well, raise the rent.

933
01:02:37,403 --> 01:02:40,273
If they can't afford it, they'll have to leave.

934
01:02:42,613 --> 01:02:46,083
I'm sure I can count on all of you. Now, let's have a drink.

935
01:02:47,713 --> 01:02:48,883
I'm counting on your support.

936
01:02:50,853 --> 01:02:52,753
That jerk.

937
01:02:53,893 --> 01:02:55,793
I am so sorry about this.

938
01:03:06,073 --> 01:03:10,273
- You scared me. - Hey, what the heck are you doing?

939
01:03:10,843 --> 01:03:12,773
What are you talking about? This is completely out of the blue.

940
01:03:13,243 --> 01:03:15,943
- What do you mean? What did I do? - Are you playing dumb?

941
01:03:16,543 --> 01:03:19,913
You gathered all the landlords with leases about to expire...

942
01:03:20,113 --> 01:03:22,053
and got them to raise the rent prices, didn't you?

943
01:03:22,353 --> 01:03:25,323
You know that's a violation of the Fair Trade Act.

944
01:03:25,393 --> 01:03:27,893
Hey, the rent going up doesn't automatically make it illegal.

945
01:03:29,463 --> 01:03:32,693
As if bleeding the elderly dry with overtreatment wasn't enough,

946
01:03:32,763 --> 01:03:36,903
you'd kick them out and threaten their livelihoods?

947
01:03:36,963 --> 01:03:38,573
Just be honest, you jerk.

948
01:03:38,873 --> 01:03:40,433
You don't care about the market, do you?

949
01:03:40,773 --> 01:03:43,743
You're scared your clinic will go under if they all leave.

950
01:03:43,803 --> 01:03:45,813
But don't you worry.

951
01:03:46,373 --> 01:03:48,113
Because you'll be leaving soon enough anyway.

952
01:03:48,613 --> 01:03:50,213
You got that call, didn't you?

953
01:03:50,713 --> 01:03:51,713
Hey, you...

954
01:03:52,353 --> 01:03:55,923
Don't tell me the real reason for this is to kick out my clinic.

955
01:03:56,123 --> 01:03:57,123
Hey.

956
01:03:57,983 --> 01:03:59,923
I'm genuinely curious about something.

957
01:04:00,423 --> 01:04:01,963
Do you think the world revolves around you?

958
01:04:03,263 --> 01:04:06,833
As your wife, Seong Mi, always says, being delusional is a sickness.

959
01:04:07,293 --> 01:04:10,403
Psychoanalytically speaking, you have an overinflated ego.

960
01:04:10,603 --> 01:04:13,203
You jerk. Do you really have to go this far?

961
01:04:13,333 --> 01:04:16,573
Hey, you'd better start looking for a new place for your clinic.

962
01:04:16,903 --> 01:04:18,943
And maybe start making some real money.

963
01:04:19,443 --> 01:04:23,243
You're not getting any younger. How long will you leech off her?

964
01:04:24,283 --> 01:04:25,283
You son of a...

965
01:04:31,423 --> 01:04:35,223
Gosh, what's with that family? I mean, they're loaded.

966
01:04:35,293 --> 01:04:38,263
If they hate seeing us so much, they should be the ones to move.

967
01:04:38,693 --> 01:04:41,063
I heard the grandfather won't leave. It's his hometown.

968
01:04:41,333 --> 01:04:44,463
Sure, Yang Dong Ik thinks it was our fault his mom left.

969
01:04:44,533 --> 01:04:47,303
So of course, he resents us. But hey, because of his family,

970
01:04:47,373 --> 01:04:48,703
I grew up without a father, so what's the big deal?

971
01:04:49,403 --> 01:04:54,043
That's true. His son's grandma and mom had affairs,

972
01:04:54,113 --> 01:04:56,583
so he was always getting teased and beat up for it.

973
01:04:57,743 --> 01:05:01,483
- I stood up for him a few times. - Yes, that's right.

974
01:05:02,383 --> 01:05:05,653
- What was that guy's name again? - Yang Hyun Bin?

975
01:05:06,423 --> 01:05:08,253
Hey! Yang Hyun Bin.

976
01:05:08,693 --> 01:05:11,463
Is that the kid who kept visiting before he left to study abroad?

977
01:05:12,593 --> 01:05:13,893
- That's him. - My gosh.

978
01:05:13,893 --> 01:05:15,603
I'm pretty sure he had a huge crush on her.

979
01:05:17,063 --> 01:05:20,833
Yes, I guess he did. Anyway, I wonder what he's up to now.

980
01:05:21,003 --> 01:05:22,443
I wonder if he even remembers me.

981
01:05:25,513 --> 01:05:28,543
(Taehan)

982
01:05:28,613 --> 01:05:31,043
(Taehan Group)

983
01:05:33,013 --> 01:05:34,053
Ju Ah.

984
01:05:35,153 --> 01:05:37,353
What's the name of the new director you'll be working for?

985
01:05:38,153 --> 01:05:41,323
Pacundo Ignacio de la Cruz Yang.

986
01:05:41,893 --> 01:05:43,723
With Yang in the name, I'm guessing it's a woman.

987
01:05:46,333 --> 01:05:50,103
- Isn't Yang the last name? - Is that it?

988
01:05:51,463 --> 01:05:53,433
Then I guess he's not a foreigner.

989
01:05:53,773 --> 01:05:54,833
Maybe he's a Korean who grew up abroad?

990
01:06:07,253 --> 01:06:11,123
It's been a while since our division was all gathered in one place.

991
01:06:11,483 --> 01:06:13,593
You've all heard the news, right?

992
01:06:18,933 --> 01:06:23,163
Meet our new General Director, who'll be joining us as of today.

993
01:06:24,033 --> 01:06:26,533
Please come in! Pacu Nacho!

994
01:06:32,873 --> 01:06:36,113
What? Who does he think he is, a movie star? So dramatic.

995
01:06:56,563 --> 01:06:57,563
Hello, everyone.

996
01:06:58,633 --> 01:07:00,033
A pleasure to meet you all.

997
01:07:01,973 --> 01:07:05,203
Nice to meet you all. Yes, it's great to meet you.

998
01:07:05,413 --> 01:07:06,543
Nice to meet you.

999
01:07:09,613 --> 01:07:10,843
(Dr. Hub)

1000
01:07:10,913 --> 01:07:13,053
(Clinic Space for Sale or Lease)

1001
01:07:13,113 --> 01:07:14,113
(Clinic Space for Sale or Lease)

1002
01:07:19,823 --> 01:07:21,493
Jeong Han!

1003
01:07:22,063 --> 01:07:24,263
Hey! You are not going to believe this.

1004
01:07:24,323 --> 01:07:26,763
Bucket is running for president of the Merchants' Association.

1005
01:07:28,133 --> 01:07:30,463
Him? President? That's completely out of left field.

1006
01:07:30,563 --> 01:07:32,433
I overheard it at the snack bar...

1007
01:07:32,573 --> 01:07:36,973
- that Bucket's running for council. - What?

1008
01:07:37,043 --> 01:07:41,813
He's scheming to become president and make the market his voter base!

1009
01:07:42,683 --> 01:07:44,483
That jerk...

1010
01:07:47,083 --> 01:07:49,983
All right, if there are no other candidates,

1011
01:07:50,983 --> 01:07:54,723
Dr. Yang Dong Ik will be considered the sole nominee,

1012
01:07:55,023 --> 01:07:56,223
and without an election,

1013
01:07:56,993 --> 01:07:59,133
he will be declared the winner.

1014
01:07:59,463 --> 01:08:02,933
Does anyone else wish to register as a candidate?

1015
01:08:05,403 --> 01:08:07,073
- All right, then. - I do.

1016
01:08:10,943 --> 01:08:12,343
- What? - What's this all of a sudden?

1017
01:08:17,213 --> 01:08:19,313
I'm running for president of the Merchants' Association.

1018
01:08:20,053 --> 01:08:22,783
Hey, are you nuts? Seong Mi will flip if she finds out.

1019
01:08:23,123 --> 01:08:24,583
Keep it down, man.

1020
01:08:25,393 --> 01:08:27,793
Well, Dr. Gong.

1021
01:08:28,793 --> 01:08:30,123
So, you're throwing your hat in the ring?

1022
01:08:32,333 --> 01:08:35,563
How do you possibly think you can handle it?

1023
01:08:37,903 --> 01:08:40,173
What's wrong? Getting cold feet?

1024
01:08:41,033 --> 01:08:43,303
Then you should just fold.

1025
01:08:50,343 --> 01:08:52,953
(Special thanks to Go Myung Hwan and Jo Seung Je)

1026
01:09:14,133 --> 01:09:16,703
(Recipe for Love)

1027
01:09:16,803 --> 01:09:18,543
It's me, the creepy stalker.

1028
01:09:18,603 --> 01:09:20,973
I believe this is the first time we've met, sir.

1029
01:09:21,973 --> 01:09:24,643
- Does Gong Ju Ah know it's you? - Again.

1030
01:09:25,013 --> 01:09:26,513
What are you going to do when Seong Mi finds out?

1031
01:09:26,683 --> 01:09:28,483
You think I can't convince her?

1032
01:09:28,483 --> 01:09:29,853
Just this once, okay?

1033
01:09:29,923 --> 01:09:31,853
When have you ever kept your word?

1034
01:09:31,923 --> 01:09:33,623
The election is next week. You really think you can win?

1035
01:09:33,693 --> 01:09:35,993
I'm the most popular guy in all of Onjeong Market.

1036
01:09:36,063 --> 01:09:38,063
Everyone hates my brother.

1037
01:09:38,123 --> 01:09:40,363
Politics isn't about what voters want.

1038
01:09:40,363 --> 01:09:42,063
It's about shaping it.

1039
01:09:42,933 --> 01:09:46,603
My dad or your dad? That is the question.

1040
01:09:46,673 --> 01:09:48,173
I'm rooting for your dad.

1041
01:09:48,233 --> 01:09:51,143
There's no point in fighting a losing battle, is there?
